From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:18:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2854/2856] drm/msm, thunderbolt: qcom: Route each USB4 DP IN adapter to
 its DP controller

The DisplayPort tunnel of the Glymur USB4 host routers was tied to
router 0 and DP controller 0: the router driver looked the controller
up by one fixed name, the DP driver refused any other controller, and
the route helper wrote one value to bits 1:0 of MDP top register 0x464,
described as "DPTX0: USB4 or native".

That register has one two-bit field per DP IN adapter, two adapters per
router (bits 1:0 and 5:4 for router 0, 9:8 and 13:12 for router 1,
17:16 and 21:20 for router 2), and the value is the DP controller that
feeds the adapter: 1 to 3 for DPTX0 to DPTX2, 0 for none. The value
written for router 0 with DPTX0 does not change.

Make the route helper take the adapter and write the calling
controller's number, cache each field for the restore after the MDP
power domain comes back, and accept DPTX0 to DPTX2 as tunnel sources.
In the router driver, give each router the DP controller that feeds its
DP IN 0 adapter: DPTX0 for router 0, DPTX1 for router 1, the pairing the
platform's Windows display driver prefers (it falls back to another
free controller; this driver does not). Router 1's DP IN registers and
mailbox codes are those of router 0.

The saved modeset state for system sleep had a single owner. Count the
owners, so that two routers with a tunnel can both go through sleep: the
first saves the state and the last one back restores it.

Tested on a Surface Laptop 8 with a Surface Thunderbolt 4 Dock and a
monitor on the dock. Through router 1 and DPTX1 the monitor runs at
3840x2160 60 Hz (8.1 Gb/s, four lanes) on plug-in in both orientations,
after a suspend rehearsal (pm_test=platform), after a suspend and at
boot. Through router 0 and DPTX0 it runs as before, on plug-in and
after a suspend rehearsal. Two tunnels at once were not tested.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
